From 9c134d41d893e2646637730a6a0623d8f0dd8aac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:37:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] [iOS] Serve all of Blink's built-in AI APIs on iOS

Summarizer, Writer, Rewriter, and Translator are served by the same
engine as `LanguageModel`, prompted as the task API polyfills of
web-ai-demos prompt the language model. `task_prompts.h` holds those
prompts, generated from the polyfills, so both builds ask the models
the same way.

LanguageDetector runs Chrome's language detection model in Blink, which
the browser serves when `ios_language_detection_model` names a copy to
bundle. Chrome downloads that model, so Chromium has none. The browser
opens it at startup, since Blink takes the model as available only once
it is open.

`-BuiltInAIKeepAwake YES` keeps the device awake, as in the WebKit build.
